# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access control (strongly recommended: the dev server listens on the LAN)
# When set, every API call, upload and photo download must carry this token.
# The web app asks for it once and remembers it in the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:password@host:3306/dbname

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM provider (optional — AI features degrade gracefully without it)
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works. Examples:
#
#   xAI Grok:
#     LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1
#     LLM_API_KEY=xai-...
#     LLM_MODEL=grok-4.6
#     LLM_VISION_MODEL=grok-4.6
#
#   Local Ollama (e.g. on a Mac mini — vision keeps photos private):
#     LLM_BASE_URL=http://192.168.x.x:11434/v1
#     LLM_API_KEY=ollama            # any non-empty string; Ollama ignores it
#     LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
#     LLM_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl
#
#   OpenAI:
#     LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#     LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
#     LLM_MODEL=gpt-4.1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=
# LLM_VISION_MODEL=

# --- Optional second provider (Provider B), for A/B comparison only.
#     Every inbox capture gets an "A/B" button that runs the same prompt on
#     both providers side by side. Base URL must be the API root only —
#     no /chat/completions suffix (the SDK appends it).
#     e.g. OpenRouter:
#     LLM2_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#     LLM2_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#     LLM2_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o
# LLM2_BASE_URL=
# LLM2_API_KEY=
# LLM2_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram inbox bot (optional). Message the bot a photo, voice note, a
# LiDAR/scan file (.usdz/.glb/.gltf/.obj/.geojson), or plain text — it lands
# in the inbox exactly like the web UI's drop zone. Production only (see
# api/boot.ts) — a dev hot-reload would otherwise start a duplicate poller.
#
#   1. Create a bot via @BotFather, copy its token.
#   2. Message the bot once, then check https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/getUpdates
#      for your chat id.
#   3. Set both vars below. Without TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS the bot refuses
#      to start at all — an allowlist-less bot accepts captures from anyone
#      who finds it, which is not what you want for a home inventory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=123456789

# --- Voice-note transcription (optional). Checked in this order:
#     1. Groq (recommended — free tier, whisper-large-v3-turbo, auto-detects
#        language per message: English/Dutch/anything Whisper supports, no
#        config needed). Get a key at https://console.groq.com — note this
#        is Groq (fast inference host), unrelated to xAI's "Grok" above
#        despite the near-identical name.
#     2. Whatever's set as the main LLM provider, if it happens to also
#        expose an OpenAI-compatible /audio/transcriptions endpoint.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo   # or whisper-large-v3 (slower, marginally more accurate)
# LLM_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=            # fallback path only — needs LLM_BASE_URL
#                                   # to expose /audio/transcriptions
